      "raw_text": "Here is the step-by-step solution to the problem:\n\n**Step 1: Determine how many cookies Suzanne made.**\nThe problem states directly that Suzanne made 36 cookies.\n$$Suzanne = 36$$\n\n**Step 2: Calculate how many cookies Josh made.**\nThe problem states that Josh made one-fourth the number of cookies that Suzanne made.\n$$Josh = \\frac{1}{4} \\times Suzanne$$\n$$Josh = \\frac{1}{4} \\times 36$$\n$$Josh = 9$$\nSo, Josh made 9 cookies.\n\n**Step 3: Calculate how many cookies Kelsie made.**\nThe problem states that Kelsie made two times more cookies than Josh.\n$$Kelsie = 2 \\times Josh$$\n$$Kelsie = 2 \\times 9$$\n$$Kelsie = 18$$\n\n**Conclusion:**\nKelsie made 18 cookies.\n\n#### 18<|im_end|>",
      "answer_text": "Here is the step-by-step solution to the problem:\n\n**Step 1: Determine how many cookies Suzanne made.**\nThe problem states directly that Suzanne made 36 cookies.\n$$Suzanne = 36$$\n\n**Step 2: Calculate how many cookies Josh made.**\nThe problem states that Josh made one-fourth the number of cookies that Suzanne made.\n$$Josh = \\frac{1}{4} \\times Suzanne$$\n$$Josh = \\frac{1}{4} \\times 36$$\n$$Josh = 9$$\nSo, Josh made 9 cookies.\n\n**Step 3: Calculate how many cookies Kelsie made.**\nThe problem states that Kelsie made two times more cookies than Josh.\n$$Kelsie = 2 \\times Josh$$\n$$Kelsie = 2 \\times 9$$\n$$Kelsie = 18$$\n\n**Conclusion:**\nKelsie made 18 cookies.\n\n#### 18",
